In South[ Sudan] the 30 year political marriage was[ fought] along national[ and] religious lines. Those in[ the] north are Arab and[ Islamic][ while] those in the south,[ the] new[ state][,][ are] African and[ Christian][.][ Keeping] them together[ proved] to be a recipe[ for] disaster.
One of the worthy sons of the African soil[,] former President Thabo Mvuyelwa Mb[eki],[ was] the main �[�]midwife” in[ the][ delivery] room of this new born[ baby].[ We][ owe] much to[ this] African despite some having tried to downplay is effort to the extent of boasting about clipping is[ wings] so that[ he] could not deliver on[ the] assignment. There is no doubt that Mb[eki][ is] wont[ to] live[ his] African dream and[ has] to be[ supported] as much as he has to be[ comm]ended for a job well done.
